ue still states that value. Wording that refuses to bargain over a value (it will not be traded, given up or changed) states that value as wanted; write \"not X\" only when the answer rejects X itself. An answer that turns away anything WITHOUT a value, or anything that does not give a value, wants that value itself: write the value, never \"without\" or \"not\" in front of it.'
